# Scenario-Based Commands

## Check Running Containers
```
docker ps
```

## Stop Container web_app
```
docker stop web_app
```

## Build Image myapi
```
docker build -t myapi .
```

## Run Web App Exposing Port
```
docker run --name web_app -p 8080:5000 -d web_app
```

## Enter Container Shell
```
docker exec -it <container_id_or_name> sh
```

## Remove Image old_api
```
docker rmi old_api
```

## Check Logs
```
docker logs <container_name>
```

## Run in Background
```
docker run -d <image>
```

## Check Which Container Uses Port 3000
```
docker ps -a --filter "publish=3000"
```

## Tag Existing Image
```
docker tag <image_id> myimage:latest
```

## Export Image to tar
```
docker save -o myimage.tar myimage
```

## Restart Container Automatically
```
docker run --restart=always -d <image>
```

## Show CPU/RAM Usage
```
docker stats
```

## Limit Memory
```
docker run -m 512m <image>
```

## Dockerfile Pre-Start Command
```
RUN <your command>
```

## Custom Nginx Image
```
docker build -t mynginx .
```
